planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:398:Eight architectural planes (section 4) implemented as a modular monolith across `engine/` (semantic kernel, commit services, governance, review, search, security), `neuron/` (interpretation, conversation, learning, agent tools), and `experience/` (native semantic UX, including the Review Panel), with Docling, the direct-baseline vLLM client, PostgreSQL extensions, and (from v0.3) Temporal as engines around the semantic core (ADR-0001 as amended by ADR-0057, sections 100 and 125; Docling-Graph was rejected with ADR-0060 on 2026-11-08, section 126). Engine packages as built through F0008 are listed in master blueprint section 77; the container topology is unchanged (`architecture/c4-container.md`). The deployable topology and dependency matrix are a P0 pre-build requirement (section 106.2).
