planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:525:No new deployable, assertion HTTP route, UI, grants or extraction activation. Current authorization's mutation facade gains optional source READ requirements in the same unit of work; it must not nest a read facade that commits the outer transaction. Existing `direct-baseline` and v1 content writer defaults follow F0005's final approved rejection decision. Full durable drops/run adoption stays F0016; full source-completeness/commit orchestration stays F0018; display stays F0022; open extraction/alignment stays F0066. New restrictions apply to attributable v2 evidence/review/correction lineage; unregistered legacy pilot references remain an explicit compatibility boundary. ADR-0065 and ADR-0075 remain Proposed until their required runtime proofs. Existing C4 topology is unchanged; feature README contains ER/component diagrams. Bounded implementation is complete: 336 unique final product cases pass and changed executable-line coverage is 1170/1266 (92.4171%). The operator approved SEC-01 only for trusted local synthetic fixtures; dependencies and resource isolation must be remediated/qualified before untrusted or production PDFs (AI Engineer + DevOps; Security verification; target 2026-11-10). Broader ADR proof/activation gates remain separate. Evidence: [PM closeout](operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-02-5a00b0ff/pm-closeout.md).
planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:554:The design schemas are `fact-slot-key-v1`, `fact-answer-v1` and `fact-slot-resolution-result-v1`. The C4 topology is unchanged, and the feature README carries the ER and component views.
planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:579:Feature run `2026-11-17-1a4ae2f0` implemented the design and was approved by the operator at G4 on 2026-11-18. It delivers migration 0014, `brain_domain.temporal`, `brain_temporal` bounds/attestation/commit/reader and the additive `/facts` changes. All 46 ACs and the six ADR-0078 proof gates pass on PostgreSQL 18 (1081 engine tests; 98.0% changed-line coverage). The operator accepted ADR-0078 on 2026-11-19 (decision run `2026-11-19-12422004`). SEC-F8-02 (the application connects as a superuser) and refusal reason persistence move to F0018. Independent review `2026-11-18-d34a095e` returned NOT DONE. Remediation run `2026-11-18-bce4909b` (approved 2026-11-19) added the commit-response temporal metadata, the legacy read shape and migration 0015 (same-slot lineage), amended S0004 AC1 and S0007 AC6, and recorded the F0018 handoffs. A second review, `2026-11-19-b21ec2de`, found that the new commit response could return a predecessor's attestation dates without READ on their documents (SEC-F8-NEW-01, High). Second remediation run `2026-11-19-8cfcd0ff` (approved 2026-11-19) refuses the whole commit with the non-disclosing 404 in that case. Evidence: [PM closeout](operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-19-8cfcd0ff/pm-closeout.md).
