planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:629:Feature run `2026-11-24-08701e37` implemented the design, with operator G4 approval on 2026-11-25. It delivers `brain_domain.provenance`, the `brain-provenance` reader (exported, not routed), the opt-in `prepare_reads` authorization hook, review-boundary preflight with refused-attempt attribution and an atomic learning reservation, and migration 0016. All 41 ACs and EX-PROV-001–005 are proven on PostgreSQL 18 (changed-line coverage 94.4%; 1392/1392 shared conformance results). G2 recorded five design corrections, among them a nullable `fact_change.from_version_id` and attempt authorization bound by `audit_event.decision_id` (see the run reports). ADR-0080 runtime proofs are met; the ADR stays Proposed pending operator acceptance. Evidence: [PM closeout](operations/evidence/runs/2026-11-24-08701e37/pm-closeout.md). F0010 owns retraction semantics; F0020/F0022/F0023 own exposure and F0041/F0026 own learning/benchmark governance.
planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:636:### 4.20 F0021 native React shell and BFF session (Phase B approved 2026-11-27)
planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:645:The [assembly plan](features/F0021-native-react-semantic-shell-and-oidc-session/feature-assembly-plan.md) and proposed [ADR-0082](architecture/decisions/ADR-0082-bff-session-runtime-and-shell-foundation.md) fix the runtime choices that ADR-0051 leaves to F0021:
planning-mds/BLUEPRINT.md:699:   - **F0021** (React shell + OIDC/session) takes the Now slot freed by F0008, as the 2026-11-10 review promised.
   236	**Accessibility, language and budget**
   237	
   238	- WCAG 2.2 AA with semantic theme tokens. All strings come from `en-US.json`.
   239	- Budget script: the entry chunk's initial JavaScript must be at most 180 kB gzip, measured from the Vite manifest.
   240	
   241	## Step 8 — Real-Browser Proof (S0009)
   242	
   243	**Stack and run conditions**
   244	
   245	- `docker-compose.e2e.yml` starts:
   246	  - PostgreSQL and authentik from the dev blueprint;
   247	  - the engine, with `BRAIN_OIDC_BACKCHANNEL_URL` pointing at `idp-recorder`;
   248	  - the built shell under `vite preview` on 4173.
   249	- Runs start from a clean volume. Results record the authentik, Chromium and Playwright versions.
   250	
   251	**Proofs**
   252	
   253	- **Token absence (S0009 AC1):** inspect cookies, every storage API, every URL, and every response body and header.
   254	- **Single refresh (AC2):** the recorder counts refresh grants per refresh-token family while 20 parallel requests run against an expired access token. The test-only `BRAIN_TEST_ACCESS_SKEW` setting is absent outside the e2e composition, and startup refuses it when `BRAIN_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` is not localhost.
   255	- **Revocation failure (AC3):** the recorder injects a 503 or a drop on `/revoke`. A follow-up refresh grant with the revoked token is refused by authentik.
   256	- **Principal isolation (AC4):** alice and bob; a list of malicious return routes.
   257	- **Mutation continuity (AC5):** a Review Panel decision is blocked by an expired session, is not received (the engine decision count is unchanged), and is sent only on "Submit now". A stale or revoked variant is refused without retry.
   258	
